{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>If Elohim will be with me.</b> To remove from me every impediment and hindrance that leads a man astray from his resolve and from the resolve of his Maker, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Eruvin 41a): three things lead a man astray from his resolve and from the resolve of his Maker — gentiles, an evil spirit, and the pressures of poverty." "<b>And will keep me.</b> From the harm of the gentiles who rise up and compel." "<b>And will give me bread to eat.</b> So that poverty does not compel me to act against my resolve and the resolve of my Maker."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Sforno cites the Talmudic phrase דקדוקי עניות; rendered 'the pressures of poverty' per standard translation of this idiom."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:13.430121564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}